# Cude.new - install layout
#
# electron-builder copies the dependency tree into the desktop package by
# walking it from the top level. pnpm's default layout keeps most packages in
# `.pnpm` and links only direct dependencies at the root, and the walk does not
# follow every edge through it: fifteen transitive packages were left out of
# the last build — `is-callable`, `hash.js`, `brorand` and the rest — so the
# packaged app started, failed to load its own server build, and served no
# routes at all.
#
# Hoisting gives the root a complete, flat tree, which is the shape
# electron-builder expects. `scripts/verify-package.mjs` fails the build if a
# package ever ships with an unresolvable dependency again.
node-linker=hoisted
